00:46:50.230 --> 00:46:53.110
because of the pandemic
and the job shortage.

00:46:53.110 --> 00:46:56.510
Or like the freezing of the fundings.

00:46:56.510 --> 00:46:58.487
But that's something that...

00:46:59.940 --> 00:47:01.170
This is where I found all the information.

00:47:01.170 --> 00:47:05.000
And then I was also cross-posting,

00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:08.401
like cross-referencing
with all the job postings

00:47:08.401 --> 00:47:09.640
that are received,

00:47:09.640 --> 00:47:13.010
because we have an excellent
announcement section

00:47:13.010 --> 00:47:13.843
on our website.

00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:19.840
I often get a ton of job
postings from the other centers.

00:47:20.120 --> 00:47:23.720
Also that is something
like if you look for jobs,

00:47:23.720 --> 00:47:26.370
that's something that
you can do looking at

00:47:28.480 --> 00:47:31.320
your university listing
or your department.

00:47:31.320 --> 00:47:32.730
They might have a section.

00:47:32.730 --> 00:47:34.970
Usually the chair of your department

00:47:34.970 --> 00:47:39.510
or your PIs receive a ton,
a ton of open positions.

00:47:39.510 --> 00:47:41.680
You might be able to ask them,

00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:44.820
so like, "Hey, if you see
anything, just forward the email."

00:47:44.820 --> 00:47:47.290
Because they usually don't
have time to read it,

00:47:47.290 --> 00:47:49.370
but if they know that you're looking...

00:47:49.370 --> 00:47:51.560
If you tell them, "Hey,
I'm considering..."

00:47:51.560 --> 00:47:54.523
I think communication with
your advisor is really key.

00:47:55.640 --> 00:47:57.610
I've seen people in conferences posting

00:47:57.610 --> 00:47:59.380
at the end of their talk:

00:47:59.380 --> 00:48:00.380
hey, I'm looking for position.

00:48:00.380 --> 00:48:01.380
I'm looking for jobs.

00:48:01.380 --> 00:48:03.150
Like it's really important to communicate

00:48:03.150 --> 00:48:04.600
what you want to do.

00:48:04.600 --> 00:48:07.920
Online presence is more
and more important,

00:48:07.920 --> 00:48:10.720
so if you have a website,
if you have a Twitter.

00:48:10.720 --> 00:48:14.970
Like the quantum Twitter is very active.

00:48:14.970 --> 00:48:16.327
It's a little bit so that you have

00:48:16.327 --> 00:48:18.750
everybody on social
media working on like...

00:48:18.750 --> 00:48:21.300
Keep working outside of
your work on social media.

00:48:21.300 --> 00:48:24.070
But it has been pretty good resources

00:48:24.070 --> 00:48:26.320
to find a job application for that.

00:48:26.320 --> 00:48:30.690
- If I can also add something
on this topic of job posting.

00:48:30.690 --> 00:48:32.910
And this has something to do with

00:48:34.088 --> 00:48:38.610
what Florian has just mentioned.

00:48:38.610 --> 00:48:39.510
Twitter.

00:48:39.510 --> 00:48:44.510
It's a great resource of
information about job postings.

00:48:45.840 --> 00:48:50.000
All the time I saw like advertisements

00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:52.800
about job postings on my area.

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:57.390
I'm not in the right moment
to apply for them yet.

00:48:57.390 --> 00:49:01.410
But if I wanted so...

00:49:01.410 --> 00:49:05.193
Just last week I saw
one amazing job posting

00:49:05.193 --> 00:49:10.193
that was just passing through my timeline.

00:49:10.770 --> 00:49:15.770
And also Twitter is basically
great for networking as well.

00:49:16.760 --> 00:49:21.070
I found my post doctoral
position through Twitter

00:49:23.143 --> 00:49:28.143
in a process of serendipity
by just clicking, clicking.

00:49:28.330 --> 00:49:32.810
And then suddenly I
found this job posting.

00:49:32.810 --> 00:49:35.363
One thing that I always recommend.

00:49:36.400 --> 00:49:40.150
Join Twitter and try to
use that professionally

00:49:40.150 --> 00:49:43.240
by having your bio describing who you are,

00:49:43.240 --> 00:49:47.610
where you went in terms
of your background.

00:49:47.610 --> 00:49:49.940
And start following people in your field,

00:49:49.940 --> 00:49:51.710
because eventually you may see

00:49:51.710 --> 00:49:54.410
on their profile a job posting

00:49:54.410 --> 00:49:56.910
that you would never find by googling

00:49:56.910 --> 00:50:00.090
or by looking at mailing lists;

00:50:00.090 --> 00:50:05.090
because on Twitter you may by
chance find such information

00:50:06.030 --> 00:50:07.360
that are quite useful.

00:50:07.360 --> 00:50:11.760
And such information comes from networking

00:50:11.760 --> 00:50:13.633
in this online environment.

